<p>Man, you hit the nail on the head.</p>
<p>I felt like this was so well done, every log had me reading further, and harder, but the payoff never happened.</p>
<p>This may be an &quot;up to the reader to decide what happened&quot; but I'd really like to know what the author meant for this to be. The swirling eye of fire is a great visual metaphor. Unfortunately, the rest of the elements don't make a lot of sense to me.</p>
<p>My question that keeps coming to mind is: Why? Why would potentially-god be stuck as an eye of fire under the arctic. This would have been such a great opportunity for something&#8230;more. Hinting of some creature, or entity, rather than just a phenominon that made someone crazy.</p>
<p>It still gets my +1 for the incredibly compelling logs, but this could have been so much more. It's promise unfullfilled.</p>

