														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4006025">
									

<p>This is one of those things that I think has to strike the right balance. An SCP doesn't have to be explained or inferable (though personally, I feel an intriguing and compelling explanation can be better than a mystery ending, but that's an opinion). Hanging your hat on &quot;we may never know&quot; can be a great result for a file&#8230;if it provides sufficient enough information for the imagination to work with a direction. The meat and potatoes of that sort of mystery comes when there's the right amount of detail to reach speculative conclusions rather than just wild guessing.</p>
<p>I feel like this one just missed the mark. Not as badly as some others I've seen, to be sure - the effort was made, you can see it was trying to get to that point, but it just never made it all the way there. I don't finish the SCP feeling like I know enough facts to have an idea what's going on - not even enough for an educated maybe - and that makes the 'use your imagination' theme fall flat. It's done well enough to avoid a downvote but not well enough for an upvote. That said, I think the author's on the right path, and I hope they hone their technique because I think they can deliver.</p>

							</div>

								
					
